.\" man/man3/Docv::Viewer::Help.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Viewer::Help" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Viewer::Help \- The help: the keys of the page view, the dock\(aqs search field and its tree as they are bound (\fB\%ACTION_HELP\fR, \fB\%FIELD_HELP\fR, \fB\%TREE_HELP\fR), and the mouse gestures, shown in the page area in place of the page, with \fB\%TITLE\fR as the heading of the title row.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Viewer::Help\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The help: the keys of the page view, the dock\(aqs search field and its
tree as they are bound (\fB\%ACTION_HELP\fR, \fB\%FIELD_HELP\fR, \fB\%TREE_HELP\fR), and
the mouse gestures, shown in the page area in place of the page, with
\fB\%TITLE\fR as the heading of the title row. It scrolls both ways.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBKEY_NAMES\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
KEY_NAMES = {
  Term::Key::ENTER => "Enter",
  Term::Key::TAB => "Tab",
  Term::Key::BACKSPACE => "Backspace",
  Term::Key::ESCAPE => "Esc",
  Term::Key::UP => "\[u2191]",
  Term::Key::DOWN => "\[u2193]",
  Term::Key::LEFT => "\[u2190]",
  Term::Key::RIGHT => "\[u2192]",
  Term::Key::PAGE_UP => "PgUp",
  Term::Key::PAGE_DOWN => "PgDn",
  Term::Key::HOME => "Home",
  Term::Key::END => "End",
  Term::Key::INSERT => "Ins",
  Term::Key::DELETE => "Del",
  \(aq \(aq.ord => "Space",
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Names of keys that are not text.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBKEYS_WIDTH = 30\fR
Widest keys column.
.TP 4
\fBMOD_NAMES\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
MOD_NAMES = [
  {Term::Mods::Ctrl, "Ctrl\-"},
  {Term::Mods::Alt, "Alt\-"},
  {Term::Mods::Super, "Super\-"},
  {Term::Mods::Shift, "Shift\-"},
]
.EE
.RE
.PP
Modifier prefixes, in the order they are written.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBMOUSE\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
MOUSE = [
  {"wheel", "scroll"},
  {"Shift\-wheel", "scroll sideways (the page or the tree)"},
  {"drag in the text", "select and copy"},
  {"double\-click a word", "select and copy it"},
  {"triple\-click", "select and copy the paragraph"},
  {"drag a thumb, click a track", "scroll"},
  {"click a link", "follow it"},
  {"click a page or group in the tree", "open it, or fold or unfold it"},
  {"click the search field", "focus it"},
  {"drag the dock\(aqs edge", "resize the dock"},
  {"click #{Frame::NAME}", "this help"},
  {"point at the page\(aqs heading", "show its source and date"},
  {"click #{Frame::CLOSE}", "quit"},
  {"back button", "back to the previous page"},
]
.EE
.RE
.PP
Mouse gestures and what they do.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBTITLE = "HELP"\fR
The heading of the title row while the help is shown.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(bindings : Bindings, field_bindings : FieldBindings, tree_bindings : TreeBindings = TreeBindings.new)\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.key_name(mods : Term::Mods, key : Int32) : String\fR
The name of a key binding: \fB\%j\fR, \fB\%Ctrl\-f\fR, \fB\%Shift\-Tab\fR, \fB\%F5\fR.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef draw(screen : Screen, frame : Frame, styles : Array(UInt16)) : Nil\fR
Draws the help in the page area of \fIframe\fR, from its first content
column scrolled by \fB\%left\fR, with the role style ids \fIstyles\fR: section
titles in \fB\%Heading1\fR, keys in \fB\%Name\fR (cut at \fB\%KEYS_WIDTH\fR), what they
do in \fB\%Text\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef keys_width : Int32\fR
Columns of the keys column and of the widest line.
.TP 4
\fBdef left : Int32\fR
Columns scrolled sideways.
.PP
\fBdef lines : Array(Docv::Viewer::Help::Line)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef max_left(frame : Frame) : Int32\fR
The largest \fB\%left\fR on \fIframe\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef max_top(frame : Frame) : Int32\fR
The largest \fB\%top\fR on \fIframe\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef rows(frame : Frame) : Int32\fR
Lines shown at once on \fIframe\fR: the content rows.
.TP 4
\fBdef scroll(delta : Int32, frame : Frame) : Nil\fR
Scrolls by \fIdelta\fR lines in the page area of \fIframe\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef scroll_x(delta : Int32, frame : Frame) : Nil\fR
Scrolls sideways by \fIdelta\fR columns in the page area of \fIframe\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef top : Int32\fR
First visible line.
.PP
\fBdef width : Int32\fR
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/viewer/help.cr
